From acf2106e758860d3313cfebd1b75df3bdabedafa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:19:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(color): characterize outputs from ICC/EDID and map
 the SDR gamut
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New output keys `color_profile` ("none" | "edid" | a matrix-shaper ICC
path) and `sdr_gamut`. A characterization feeds the panel's colorimetry
(colorants, white, TRC); `sdr_gamut = "srgb"` opts into interpreting
untagged SDR as sRGB and mapping it into that colorimetry, which confines
it to the sRGB gamut — the fix for oversaturation on wide-gamut panels.
The default `sdr_gamut = "native"` stages no output transform at all:
pixels stay identical to today even with a profile set. The mapping rides
the scene's supplied color transform (FP16 path; direct scanout is then
correctly disabled); HDR mode is untouched.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
